<title>FRANCE: Metaleurop cuts zinc price.</title>
<headline>Metaleurop cuts zinc price.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>French metals group Metaleurop SA, a unit  of Preussag, said on Friday it had cut its indicative zinc price to  10,780 francs per tonne from 11,980 francs.</p>
<p>The move partly retraces two price hikes in the past week which had  been driven by fluctuations in the value of zinc and the dollar.</p>
<p>Zinc reached a seven-year high on the London Metal Exchange earlier  this week, powered by strong fundamentals and a reduction in stocks.  teh</p>
